    "Upright only uses temporary button diversion, so nothing is written to the mouse’s memory. Turning the mouse off and on always restores its factory behavior." : {

    },
    "Upright sends keyboard shortcuts, media keys and clicks on behalf of your mouse. Until you allow it, mapped buttons keep their normal behavior." : {

    },
    "Upright talks to the mouse with the publicly documented HID++ 2.0 protocol, using temporary button diversion from the REPROG_CONTROLS_V4 feature (0x1B04). It does not include or depend on any Logitech software." : {

